cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ComponentBench, please cite the following work."
title: "ComponentBench: Diagnosing Component-Level Failures in Computer-Use Agents"
abstract: >
  ComponentBench is a diagnostic benchmark for computer-use agents that
  targets the middle layer between atomic GUI grounding and long-horizon
  workflow benchmarks. It evaluates agents on individual UI component
  interactions across 97 canonical component types, 14 interaction families,
  and 3 React libraries (Ant Design, MUI, Mantine), with 2,910 programmatically
  verified tasks in the Full benchmark and 912 newly generated hard tasks in
  the Core benchmark.
